      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Hard-hitting critiques often focus on the macroeconomic instability caused by large, persistent fiscal deficits required to fund expansive social programs. High taxation, when significantly increased, can demonstrably trigger capital flight as businesses and wealthy individuals move investments to lower-tax jurisdictions. These models often underestimate the inflationary pressures that result from massive, state-driven demand increases without corresponding increases in productive supply. Essentially, the projected funding mechanisms struggle to sustain the promised expenditure levels without triggering significant market distortions or debt crises.",
      "source": "target",
